  "notes": "Church (6×10, D-054): a warm-stone church in its walled churchyard — the nave on a plinth with buttresses and tall windows under a terracotta gable roof, a transept with a rose window, a round apse with a conical roof at the back and a square front tower with belfry openings, a clock and a terracotta spire topped by a brass cross over the arched door; around it graves with headstones in rows, cypresses and trees, a paved path through a roofed lych gate in the low stone wall and a bench. Service building: no cart, chimney or smoke.",
